   <h3> Runja</h3>
   <p>
   
Member since: Thu Mar 30, 2000<br>
was last logged in: Sat Mar 31, 2001 at 17:27



<p><b>Full name:</b> Runja Blackblood


<br><b>Profile:</b>
Level 55 Male Troll Shaman


<br><b>Religion:</b>
Innoruuk

<br><b>Hord Rank:</b>
Warlord



<p><b>Runja's Bio:</b>
<table border=1 width=400>
  <tr><td>
  Born an orphan and not knowing his heritage, Runja was raised by the great
troll shaman Kaglari.  Kaglari taught Runja the secrets of the shaman.  He
learned to extract the poisons from the snakes in the swamp, and he studied
the diseases of the mummies in the desert.  Along the way, he learned the
power of hate from the priests in the temple of Innoruuk.  As Runja grew, so
did the hate within him.

<p>
One day Runja went to Kaglari and asked if there was anything she needed.
Kaglari was working on a new potion of great power.  With an evil glare,
she looked at Runja and said "Bringz me da blood of dem Dervish Cuthroats!".
Runja was shocked by the request as he knew that the Dervish were more
powerful than he and that the request meant certain death.  As he was about
to question Kaglari's request, he looked into Kaglari's glare and felt his
hate explode.  Runja felt something he had never experienced before.  It
was an unexplainable feeling that he must travel to the Southern Desert
of Ro.

<p>Alone and weary Runja arrived at the Desert of Ro.  On reaching the
Dervish camp, Runja began to prepare for his battle.  Suddenly he heard a
voice behind him.  Turning around, he saw a war torn troll shaman.
Her eyes glared with much wisdom and fear.  

<p>She spoke forth "Zhokaii needz Dervish ringz.  Yooz wanna help Zhokaii?"

<p>Knowing that her help would nearly guarantee that he would be able to
obtain the blood for Kaglari and also figuring that he could probably learn
some more of the arcane secrets of the shaman, Runja grinned evilily.  "Yez!
me will helpz yooz keel dese worthless Dervisheez!".

<p>The battle lasted many hours.  When it was over 40 dervish had fallen
at the feet of Runja and Zhokaii.  Zhokaii was impressed with the capabilities
of such a young troll.  She could easily see the burning hate and desire
within Runja.  

<p>Speaking with Zhokaii, Runja learned that she is the leader and
Warlord of the great Bloodhorde guild.  Seeing such promise in
a young troll, Zhokaii invited Runja to join the ranks of the horde.  Runja
quickly accepted the offer and joined the Bloodhorde family.

<p>Upon returning to Grobb, Runja ran to Kaglari to deliver the blood that
he had obtained.  Curious as to how Runja managed to defeat the Dervish,
Kaglari inquired as to how he was able to obtain the blood.  Runja then
told her of Zhokaii and how he is now a minion within the ranks of the
Bloodhorde.  Kaglari stared at Runja with much hate.  Then an evil smile
broke across her face.  "Yooz habe grown much young Runja.  Yooz work iz
dun here.  Go forth an make da horde more powerful!".  At that command,
Runja stocked up on supplies and headed out to the unknown areas of Norrath
to hunt with his new family of evil.

<p>Many years passed.  Runja continued to grow and increase in rank within
Bloodhorde.  The horde was growing and the future seemed to bode greatness
for the horde.  When without warning, Zhokaii announced that she has grown
too old and weary for battle and is unable to lead the horde any longer.
This put Bloodhorde into chaos.  Zhokaii had been the cornerstone of
Bloodhorde.

<p>After several weeks of watching the events within the guild, Zhokaii came
forth and talked of a new leader for Bloodhorde.  She told a story in which
she long ago gave birth to a son.  She had to hide this son for fear that he
would be the target of the enemies of the Horde and a weakness for her.  She
said that this son has been amoung the horde.

<p>At that point the members of Bloodhorde realized who their new leader was.
It was destinity that Runja would rise to lead the mighty Bloodhorde.
